 "ai": {
  "analysis": [
   "[Google Gemini] Breakout strategies on lower timeframes (5m/15m) suffer from low win rates (30-38%) due to false breakouts in choppy, counter-trend market regimes.",
   "[Google Gemini] High volume ratio (>1.1-1.3) alone does not prevent false breakouts if HTF trend alignment or volatility compression signals (e.g. low ATR percentile or ADX threshold) are missing.",
   "[Google Gemini] Trades failing the win-rate check often suffer from wide ATR stops (3.0-3.5 ATR) that allow deep pullbacks into consolidation zones before failing.",
   "[Google Gemini] Requiring HTF trend confirmation (htf:1h:trend == 1) and strong bar closing power (closepos >= 0.70) significantly reduces low-quality breakout signals.",
   "[Groq (free tier)] Low‑timeframe signals often lose because stops are set too tight (fees eat the profit) and they lack higher‑timeframe trend confirmation.",
   "[Groq (free tier)] Breakout strategies on 5m/15m bars suffer from frequent split‑time losses, indicating they trigger on noisy moves without volume or trend filters.",
   "[Groq (free tier)] Inside‑pullback ideas perform poorly when the price is against the dominant higher‑timeframe trend, leading to counter‑trend entries.",
   "[Groq (free tier)] Adding multi‑timeframe trend checks and modest volume/ATR filters can filter out choppy, low‑volatility setups while keeping daily signal count.",
   "[Google Gemini] Breakout strategy variants suffer from low win rates (<38%) due to entering during weak or counter-HTF market regimes.",
   "[Google Gemini] Adding mandatory 4H HTF trend alignment (htf:4h:trend == 1) ensures trades flow with macro momentum, filtering out chop.",
   "[Google Gemini] Requiring ADX > 20/25 or volume expansion (volr > 1.2) ensures sufficient momentum to hit profit targets before pullbacks hit tight stops.",
   "[Groq (free tier)] Many losers are from tiny ATR stops that get eaten by fees; larger ATR or swing stops can reduce stop‑loss noise."
